  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (8t+{e}^{t-2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+{e}^{t-2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=5.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =4({2}^{2})+{e}^{2-2}+C \\\\ 5 & =16+1+C \\\\ 5 & =17+C \\\\ C & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=4{t}^{2}+{e}^{t-2}-12.$",
